{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1420,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nuclear waste. We’ve got a lot of it, it'll\nstay dangerous for tens of thousands of years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5900,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we don't really know what to do with it.\nSo why don't we just send it into space and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9800,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crash it into the sun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11160,
    "dDurationMs": 4510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, first, it's really dangerous to put\nnuclear waste on a rocket, since rockets have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15670,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a tendency to occasionally explode while launching,\nmaking any nuclear-waste-filled exploding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20800,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rocket into a really big dirty bomb."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22970,
    "dDurationMs": 5309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the bigger reason is that it's actually\nreally really hard to *get* to the sun. It"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28279,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might seem like it should be easy, since the\nsun's gravity is always pulling us towards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32730,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it. But we're also orbiting really fast sideways\naround the sun, so that as we fall towards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37530,
    "dDurationMs": 1119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it, we miss it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38649,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In order to crash _into_ the sun, you have\nto slow down so that you're _not_ going sideways"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42749,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really fast. The earth - and everything on\nit - is moving around the sun at around 30"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46889,
    "dDurationMs": 4781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kilometers per second, so you'd have to accelerate\nto a speed of 30kilometers per second backwards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51670,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away from the earth in order to stop moving\naround the sun and do a sun dive. And you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56019,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to slow down all the way – with even\na little bit of sideways speed, you'll miss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60219,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun and whip around, not crashing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62549,
    "dDurationMs": 6621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so a speed of 30 kilometers per second\nis really fast, but just how fast? Well, from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69170,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earths’s orbit, you only need to be going\n_11_ kilometers per second faster than the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72770,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earth in order to escape from the entire solar\nsystem. Which means that it's much, much harder"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77640,
    "dDurationMs": 5799,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to crash into the sun than to escape it altogether.\nLet me say that again: it takes less acceleration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83439,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get to _other_ stars than it does to get\nto our own sun. Crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87500,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it gets weirder: because the gravity from\nan object is stronger the closer you are to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92840,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it, the smaller your orbit is, the faster\nyour orbital speed. For example, Mercury goes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97820,
    "dDurationMs": 4719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around the sun at a speed one and a half times\nfaster than earth, while Pluto goes only a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102539,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sixth as fast. And that means it's actually\nway harder to crash into the sun from Mercury"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107259,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than from the earth, even though you're closer,\nbecause you'd have to accelerate to a speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111009,
    "dDurationMs": 5210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 48 kilometers per second backwards instead\nof 30. And it's way _easier_ to crash into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116219,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun from Pluto, since you only have to\naccelerate to a speed of five kilometers per"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120289,
    "dDurationMs": 750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second backwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121039,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if you're trying to crash into the\nsun just using rockets, it's far more efficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125869,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to first go to the outer solar system where\nyour speed is much lower, then do a second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130259,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burn to counteract that slow orbital speed\nand allow you to fall directly into the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134879,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's precisely why early mission trajectories\nfor NASA's spacecraft to study the sun proposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140129,
    "dDurationMs": 5161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going out to Jupiter first – to make it\neasier to slow down and get to the sun. Ultimately"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145290,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they decided instead to use repeated flyby's\nof Venus to slow down the probe and save on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149840,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rocket fuel getting to the sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151780,
    "dDurationMs": 5709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how gravity assists work is a topic for\nanother day. Speaking of which – how long"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157489,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would a day be on the sun?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
